{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKLTcbDB1hCxM6Dx3jb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Fix first: show whether the change worked, and when it takes effect\n\nThe most likely cause of the \"did my bank change work?\" calls is Steps 2 and 3. After submitting, customers get a vague \"Request received\" with no date. The next morning the dashboard still shows the old account ending 4417. That looks exactly like a failure. Bacs mandate changes normally take several working days, so the system may be working fine, but nothing tells the customer that.\n\n**Sprint scope:**\n1. **Confirmation page:** Say \"Your new account ending XXXX will be used from your [date] payment of £X. Your [earlier date] payment will still come from the account ending 4417.\" Send the same message by email. Bacs rules already require you to confirm a new mandate, so this may just be a matter of showing that content on screen.\n2. **Dashboard:** Show both accounts during the switch, e.g. \"Changing to account ending XXXX, active from [date].\" Never show only the old account with no explanation.\n3. **Check this first:** Confirm that the old account still showing is a normal processing delay, not a failed update. If it's failing, that bug comes before everything else.\n\n**Next, if there's time (small changes):**\n- **Sort code field:** Accept 12-34-56 and spaces by stripping the dashes and spaces. Check each field as the customer types and name the problem (\"Sort code must be 6 digits\"). Never clear what they've entered. Clearing the account number on every error makes people give up.\n- **Buttons:** Make Submit the primary button (filled, brand colour) and Cancel secondary (a text link or outline). Two identical grey buttons invite mis-clicks.\n\n**Measure:** Count the \"did my change work?\" calls for a few weeks before and after release."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3191,"cache_read_input_tokens":5140,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3191},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50ca2a48-78a6-4d40-9de8-29eae02833e4","uuid":"dc2eba46-05c9-4242-b7a8-436f1e646551","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:26:22.178Z","request_id":"req_011CftKLTNDBfP2RY4BAnLLd"}
